  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Jus 1401.05 Institutional lender",
  "priorExpiration": "2019-04-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Jus 1401.05 “Institutional lender” means “institutional lender” as defined in RSA 356-B:3, XVII, namely “one or more commercial or savings banks, savings and loan associations, trust companies, credit unions, industrial loan associations, insurance companies, pension funds, or business trusts including but not limited to real estate investment trusts, any other lender regularly engaged in financing the purchase, construction, or improvement of real estate, or any assignee of loans made by such a lender, or any combination of any of the foregoing entities.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Jus 1400) #9783-A, eff 9-11-10, EXPIRED: 9-11-18\n\nNew. #12657, INTERIM, eff 11-1-18, EXPIRED: 4-30-19\n\nNew. #12910, eff 10-24-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/jus1400.html"
